The module validates an unknown value as a recursive command tree. Export the existing `CommandNode` interface and `validateCommandTree` function without changing their signatures. A valid node is a non-array object with exactly the required `name` and `run` properties plus optional `children`. `name` must be a nonempty string, `run` must be a function, and `children`, when present, must be an array of nodes. Extra properties are allowed. Validate children in index order and return every error without mutating input. Paths begin with `root`; errors must use exactly `"<path>: expected object"`, `"<path>.name: expected nonempty string"`, `"<path>.run: expected function"`, or `"<path>.children: expected array"`. Do not descend into a malformed `children` value. Empty input arrays are valid when encountered as children. Shared node objects are validated at every location; cyclic references must produce `"<path>: cycle detected"` at the edge that re-enters the current ancestor chain.

